cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Shunyaya Arithmetic Origin Resolution (SAOR), please cite the project using these metadata. Software is Apache-2.0; documentation is separately licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0 as described in LICENSE."
title: "Shunyaya Arithmetic Origin Resolution (SAOR)"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Shunyaya Framework Authors"
version: 1.3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OMPSHUNYAYA/Shunyaya-Arithmetic-Origin-Resolution"
url: "https://github.com/OMPSHUNYAYA/Shunyaya-Arithmetic-Origin-Resolution"
abstract: >-
  Shunyaya Arithmetic Origin Resolution develops an exact arithmetic theory
  of realization behaviour under common prime context. Its v1.3.0 results
  include a general finite critical-support synthesis theorem, an anchored-cone
  corollary for every distinct equal-sum/equal-product pair, and a sharp
  complete future classifier with unique minimum critical support {5,7,11}.
keywords:
  - arithmetic realization
  - equal sum and product
  - retained-factor transfer
  - critical support
  - context resolution
  - exact classification
  - verification
license: Apache-2.0
